{"title":"General Relativity","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>General relativity deals with spacetime and its behavior when an object has any behavior. It deals with things that the Special Theory of Relativity can not deal with.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Concepts\">Concepts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=General_Relativity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Concepts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In General Relativity, spacetime is a 4D differentiable <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Manifold\" title=\"Manifold\">Riemannian manifold</a> whose curvature tensor satisfies Einstein’s field equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/052236848e59f53926ee459416985f83238157fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R_{\\mu\\nu} - \\frac{1}{2}Rg_{\\mu\\nu} = \\frac{8\\pi G}{c^4}T_{\\mu\\nu}.\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>In this <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partial_differential_equation&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Partial differential equation (page does not exist)\">system of PDEs</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/128bf259fef6443cc1d708e731ca4b42e2556c9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R_{\\mu\\nu}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ricci_curvature_tensor&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Ricci curvature tensor (page does not exist)\">Ricci curvature tensor</a>, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a summed version of the Ricci curvature tensor. The entire left hand side is sometimes known as the Einstein tensor for this reason. On the right-hand side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c29f86228c38ae27f1d641827ed89eadeba8bdaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{\\mu\\nu}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> is the mass-energy tensor, which describes the distribution of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mass-energy&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mass-energy (page does not exist)\">mass-energy</a> throughout the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Universe&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Universe (page does not exist)\">universe</a>, and the constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509c37a54d9fb0278dc182edd69af87bf204a3ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8\\pi G}{c^4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"36\" height=\"37\" /> is chosen so that General Relativity reduces to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Classical_Mechanics\" title=\"Classical Mechanics\">Newtonian mechanics</a> in the low-mass, low-velocity limit.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Predictions\">Predictions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=General_Relativity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Predictions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Successful predictions of General Relativity include:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Gravitational lensing</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Black_hole&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Black hole (page does not exist)\">Black holes</a></li>\n<li>Gravitational time dilation</li>\n<li>The precession of Mercury’s orbit</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=General_Relativity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Albert_Einstein\" title=\"Albert Einstein\">Albert Einstein</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Physics\" title=\"Physics\">Physics</a>\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=General_Relativity&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192219\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 47/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 938/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.788      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.788      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17712:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192219 and revision id 137928. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}